    "doc_text": "XIN_ENG_20051118.0124\n\nBAGHDAD, Nov. 18 , 2005 (Xinhua)\n\n1st lead: Blasts at Shiite mosques kill 56 in eastern Iraq\n\n\n\n\nTwo suicide bombing attacks on Shitte mosques in eastern Iraq killed at least 56 people and wounded scores of others on Friday, CNN reported.\n\nTwo suicide bombers blew themselves up in two Shiite mosques in the town of Khanaqin in eastern Iraq, when people were conducting their Friday prayers, the police said.\n\nKhanaqin is a Shiite-dominated town in the northeast of Baghdad, with Sunnis and Kurds living there.\n\nReports reaching here from Khanaqin said that local authorities have immediately imposed a curfew in the town near the Iranian border.",
